{"id":19703,"title":"Représentation et algorithmes pour l'exploration interactive de volumes procéduraux étendus et détaillés","url":"https://inria.hal.science/inria-00598406v1","final_url":"https://inria.hal.science/inria-00598406/document","year":2007,"kind":"paper","source":"hal","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"9134d5cc21a8c0123f37d81f46f277e339cb09e70c94170dc2d378d5ebdfa1e1","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793059462.3369346,"text_chars":155879,"abstract":"Les scènes naturelles sont souvent a la fois très riches en détails et spatialement vastes. Dans ce projet, on s'intéresse notamment a des données volumiques de type nuage, avalanche, écume. L'industrie des effets spéciaux s'appuie sur des solutions logicielles de rendu de gros volumes de voxels, qui ont permis de très beau résultats, mais a très fort coût en temps de calcul et en mémoire. Réciproquement, la puissance des cartes graphiques programmable (GPU) entraine une convergence entre le domaine du temps réel et du rendu réaliste, cependant la mémoire limitée des cartes fait que les données volumiques représentables en temps réel restent faibles (5123 est un maximum). Proposer des structures et algorithmes adaptées au GPU permettant un réel passage a l'échelle, et ainsi, de traiter interactivement ce qui demande actuellement des heures de calcul, est le défi que ce projet cherche a relever.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://inria.hal.science/inria-00598406/document","https://inria.hal.science/inria-00598406v1","https://artis.inrialpes.fr/Publications/2007/CN07/","https://gigavoxels.inria.fr/Publications/2007/CN07/"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1272-tetrahedral-surface-extraction-livnat-et-al-optimization.md","name":"Tetrahedral Surface Extraction (Livnat et al. Optimization)","k":12},{"path":"2010-flat-blocking-multi-resolution.md","name":"Flat Blocking Multi-resolution","k":2},{"path":"2191-min-max-grid.md","name":"Min-Max Grid","k":2},{"path":"927-emission-absorption-model.md","name":"Emission-Absorption Model","k":5},{"path":"2082-zero-order-integration-rectangle-rule.md","name":"Zero Order Integration (Rectangle Rule)","k":2},{"path":"4575-gpu-k-d-tree-ray-traversal.md","name":"GPU K-D Tree Ray Traversal","k":1},{"path":"5023-ordered-list-generation-via-n3-tree-traversal.md","name":"Ordered List Generation via N3-Tree Traversal","k":1},{"path":"3950-regular-grid.md","name":"Regular Grid","k":3},{"path":"4594-volumetric-occlusion-culling-via-occlusion-queries.md","name":"Volumetric Occlusion Culling via Occlusion Queries","k":1},{"path":"1587-octree-traversal.md","name":"Octree Traversal","k":7},{"path":"2532-3d-texture-proxy-geometry-3d-texture-proxy-view-aligned-slic.md","name":"3D Texture Proxy Geometry — 3D Texture Proxy, View-Aligned Slices, 3D-Texture Volume Rendering, 3D Texture-Based Volume Rendering","k":2},{"path":"4571-lru-cache-management-for-voxel-bricks.md","name":"LRU Cache Management for Voxel Bricks","k":1},{"path":"5202-stackless-traversal.md","name":"Stackless Traversal","k":1},{"path":"3377-two-pass-depth-ray-casting.md","name":"Two-Pass Depth Ray Casting","k":1},{"path":"4573-adaptive-sampling-step-with-early-ray-termination.md","name":"Adaptive Sampling Step with Early Ray Termination","k":1},{"path":"2854-pre-integration-lookup.md","name":"Pre-Integration Lookup","k":1},{"path":"2191-deepbrick.md","name":"DeepBrick","k":2},{"path":"851-hierarchical-trilinear-ray-casting.md","name":"Hierarchical Trilinear Ray Casting","k":3},{"path":"1272-post-classification-transfer-function-sampling.md","name":"Post-classification Transfer Function Sampling","k":4},{"path":"1555-distance-to-hypertextures.md","name":"Distance to Hypertextures","k":1},{"path":"6344-n3-tree-with-regular-mipmapped-bricks.md","name":"N3-tree with regular mipmapped bricks","k":1},{"path":"4755-brick-lod-selection.md","name":"Brick LOD Selection","k":1},{"path":"2624-hidden-volume-removal-using-hierarchical-occlusion-maps.md","name":"Hidden Vo